<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Images with Alt Text</title>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>Images with Alt Text</h1>
    <p>Examples of images using the HTML alt attribute.</p>

    <h2>Mountain Image</h2>
    <img
        src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1464822759023-fed622ff2c3b?w=500"
        alt="Snow-covered mountains under a clear sky"
        width="400"
    >

    <h2>Nature Image</h2>
    <img
        src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1441974231531-c6227db76b6e?w=500"
        alt="Sunlight shining through a green forest"
        width="400"
    >

    <h2>River Image</h2>
    <img
        src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1437482078695-73f5ca6c96e2?w=500"
        alt="A peaceful natural landscape"
        width="400"
    >

    <h2>Image with Missing Source</h2>
    <img
        src="missing-image.jpg"
        alt="Placeholder for an image that cannot be loaded"
        width="400"
    >

    <p>
        The alt attribute provides alternative text when an image
        cannot load and helps screen readers describe images to users.
    </p>

</body>
</html>